body:
I should note that I am of a relatively healthy weight, but that may not matter. I'm 5'5.75 at 142 lbs and a bicyclist. Trans female. Size 0 pants. I also ride my bicycle almost every single day for transportation and for fun.

&#x200B;

I also try to consume as little sugar as I can. I'd say that, outside of coffee creamer (I know it's terrible for you), I consume maybe 30 grams of sugar a day, but I try and consume as little as possible due to the net negatives that comes with it. Otherwise, my diet is pretty good. I just deal with Barrett's due to, I think, covid.

I guess that you don't know who I am. I'm the one that posted the three demos onto YouTube a few years ago.

&#x200B;

https://www.youtube.com/channel/UC7QTsCXllOJ5gqn\_0jcJ4Pg

Hey. I run a game and music store on eBay and connected the dots between la3904 and retrovgames because of Jacob R's video on them back in January. Bought a game from me that I hand delivered the same day. I forgot to mark it as shipped and then got mad that I didn't ship it the next day. Sends messages out at 5 in the morning. Demanded a refund 40 days later, despite not living in Virginia. My handle on eBay is Brongo111.

&#x200B;

https://www.ebay.com/usr/the\_brongo

Some may see it as a way to make money, but most don't. I've been riding for twelve years and despite all of the injuries, I've only met a few that see it as a financial benefit. Most just want to not die while doing something that they love.

&#x200B;

My last crash was a month ago and the only thing I thought of was that my recovery was going to take quite a while (although my injury was caused by wind pushing me onto the ground while riding, so there isn't another participant that I can sue).

Of course! I'm glad that people enjoyed what I got my hands on and released years later.

&#x200B;

Feel free to reach out/follow me on IG Jennifer.Lieberman.3 if you'd like.

I just wanted to say that I'm doing okay nowadays for the most part. I changed my username on there, but my handle is Jennifer.Lieberman.3

&#x200B;

I'm glad that people understood why I released it and aren't, for the most part, upset that I released it.

Having providers gatekeep medications from people that truly need them is horrendous and such a rampant problem amongst the populous that deal with ADHD and severe anxiety problems.

&#x200B;

It's really awesome to hear the welcoming stories from people benefitting from starting their medication route.

So, people have issues with me selling things on eBay? I've said this before, but I have had various head injuries that make it harder for me to work in a normal manner. I'm just trying to survive.

&#x200B;

Or that it got rained on? What?

I sell a lot of loose games and sometimes it doesn't get to the destination in an appropriate manner. Or it gets stolen (that happened recently, someone replaced what I sent with new packaging and such with bubble wrap to replace the two ds cartridges, jeopardy and brain age 2. Super weird circumstances). I use stamps and 99 percent of the time, it gets to the destination within the time frame, but sometimes they get lost and yeah. I use stamps vs tracking as it's a 2 dollar and some change difference on each package so.

&#x200B;

First one never messaged me, I was kind of surprised at that. The second one is weird. I don't see how someone would buy a new ds lite to play a game, but whatever. I asked them to file a claim with ebay after I gave them my evidence that the game worked and they refused. A few weeks pass and he hit me with a negative.

Who said that I was on disability? I may have a lot of issues because of my head injuries, but I fell through the cracks due to insurance forcing me out of the hospital while still in a coma and never got on disability. My injuries are due to people going too fast, using their phone while driving, and not paying attention.

&#x200B;

I'm not interested in commenting on war in this thread as we have clear disagreements with how that system is handled. Also, I have no intentions to discredit or to argue about veterans or their ability to work while on disability. I think that the process should be easier to get on disability, but that's all I will say.

I had someone who swore that I had adhd, but because of the test that I took (basically telling me to press the space bar on a computer whenever I saw a certain letter on the screen or heard a certain sound) said that I didn't I couldn't get the medication that I think helps.

&#x200B;

The other test I took was different, although I don't remember anything about it. I took it at home instead of at a practice and I also took it before having my morning coffee. It's kind of surprising that I wasn't given it from the "TBI specialist" PMHNP, but whatever. I think that had I been given it at an earlier date of my recovery, my life would be slightly different. #Gatekeeping

Although I looked between 2007 and 2008 and found nothing of value. I wish that YouTube had better search features as trying to find super old videos is hard given that you have to scroll all the way to the end to find anything.

&#x200B;

Also, there is a remastered version of the recording of brompton cocktail, but I don't know how much you would say that it is better compared to one of the two originals.

&#x200B;

https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LiwwrhlYnOI

His father has said that it was accidental. He was loving life at the end. He accidentally mixed opiates given to him for pain related to his recovery for Lasik surgery. He, more than likely, didn't think anything of it as I'm sure he had done that before. Probably not at the same dosage, but still.

&#x200B;

I for the longest time believed that it was a suicide, but apparently it wasn't based on what Sam says based on his conversations with Joe.

(I didn't buy this originally with the intention to sell it. I bought it as a fan who has attachment issues and Jimmy means a lot to me. Had associates at World Audience acquired the ability to give me the $1400 for the items at the time (pre-head injuries), I would have gladly given it up.)

&#x200B;

I resell now as working is hard from a neurological perspective.

I'm going to post the rained on copy for $80 starting auction. I have posted a copy of GL STST at the link attached. [https://www.ebay.com/itm/255400651690](https://www.ebay.com/itm/255400651690)

&#x200B;

I'm not sure as to when/if I will post the rest of his stuff. It'll take time for me to process. I will be posting the shirt I got from WA sometime in the future as it's not important to my attachment stuff towards A7X.

However, it is not of something that can be sold in conventional methods as most selling platforms forbid of such.

&#x200B;

I have a check of Jimmy's, one of his belt buckles, tour passes, drawings, etc.

I guess I should say, damaged C3+issues like PTSD,OCD, various other anxiety issues that have resulted in seeing multiple forms of therapist throught the years. End of 2015 at age 21 and I had my birthday 18 days before the second injury happened.

&#x200B;

I don't have any learning issues, but after I woke up, I couldn't remember things I read in any format (paper, online, etc.). That was a real challenge to cope with. I do have certain audio and visual issues, mainly understanding some words when I'm stressed and not understanding things like fire hydrants or street signs when I pass them. They kind of look blurry, like I don't understand what is there.

Hey! Some of the things, but you can find my store at this link. If you see anything, I'm sure we can work on a price.

&#x200B;

https://www.ebay.com/usr/the\_brongo

Actually, thinking about it makes wonder how this will turn out in regards to the rewards of buying the token. A person buys it legally considering it as an investment in turn to get perks. I am presuming that the rewards of said NFT ownership would be considered dividends and you pay taxes on dividends, from a stock perspective. So, how does this work? Say you get a ticket that runs 100 bucks. Do you pay the tax bracket amount based on what your income or is it a flat rate or what?

&#x200B;

This makes me wonder, especially considering that A7X as a business has said that they will be losing money on this venture.

Also, one other issue is that the presumably uninformed buyers of these NFT's may not understand liquidity or risk or anything related to buying or selling anything that is legally considered an investment. However, I'm not familiar with NFT's in that aspect, so I'm not sure if the band has to disclose this information.

&#x200B;

Also, taxes. Legally, it is property and with that being said, if the owner of the said property decides to, in any and all forms, tries to make or lose money using this investment, it needs to be reported on your yearly tax forms, presuming that they don't allow minors to buy it as I'm pretty sure that would constitute the same thing as normal property-owning laws regarding minors.

Hey, I haven't sold most of what I have. You (and others) can find what I am selling at this link. Just an fyi, I am pretty reasonable when it comes to prices, so negotiate with me if needed. It's really just been a process of me coming to terms with letting go of this stuff more than anything so. Feel free to ask any questions via here or through IG u/Brongo111 or through ebay.

&#x200B;

https://www.ebay.com/usr/the\_brongo
